\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Alexander\'92s men had the gate. They also had the security office, the perimeter controls and several unanswered calls to the man whose orders they were now following.\
The lieutenant commanding the entrance had watched the Christmas Special on his device. He had applauded the verdict, admired the sharks and been personally offended when three women interrupted the execution. Now they had taken Alexander, and the UDF was offering to help recover him.\
He accepted.\
On the security console, he authorised the approaching troops and vehicles. The roadside weapons swivelled away. The UDF lieutenant watched them settle before stepping onto the gravel.\
He crossed with all his toes. His soldiers followed.\
The two lieutenants shook hands.\
\'93They\'92ve taken Mr Shakti underground,\'94 the Shakti officer said. \'93We\'92re trying to find out where.\'94\
His visitor accepted this information and moved aside for an armoured carrier. The Shakti lieutenant waved it through, then waved through the next vehicle and directed soldiers towards the forecourt.\
He had expected to spend the evening keeping the UDF out. Letting it in was turning out to be much easier.\
More of Alexander\'92s supporters came forward to explain what had happened in the auditorium. One had nearly shot Hayley. Another had recognised the undead son before anyone else. A third had stood directly behind Alexander during the applause and wanted to know whether the UDF had recorded the show.\
They had.\
He supplied his contact details.\
A guard inspected a passing soldier\'92s rifle and clicked his tongue.\
\'93We stopped buying those years ago.\'94\
The soldier looked at the weapon slung across the guard\'92s chest. He had seen one in a recruitment presentation, shortly before discovering the presentation concerned a different career.\
\'93Good, are they?\'94\
The guard lifted it for inspection.\
\'93You have no idea.\'94\
The soldier took an appreciative look, then caught up with his section. Behind him, the guard resumed explaining to a colleague how close he had come to saving Alexander.\
The vehicles kept coming. The Shakti lieutenant found room for them, pleased to have obtained so much assistance without first having to consult anyone.\
